<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for Bouncy Cars, published by PerianDevelopment.">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#101827">
  <title>Privacy Policy | Bouncy Cars — PerianDevelopment</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --page: #f4f6fa;
      --surface: #ffffff;
      --ink: #172033;
      --muted: #5d687b;
      --line: #e3e8f0;
      --accent: #315fe8;
      --accent-soft: #edf2ff;
      --max: 860px;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--page);
      color: var(--ink);
      font: 16px/1.7 system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    }
    .topbar {
      height: 8px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, #315fe8, #6c8cff);
    }
    main {
      width: min(calc(100% - 32px), var(--max));
      margin: 52px auto;
    }
    .document {
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 20px;
      box-shadow: 0 12px 36px rgba(23, 32, 51, .06);
      padding: clamp(26px, 6vw, 58px);
    }
    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: .78rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.2rem);
      line-height: 1.12;
      letter-spacing: -.045em;
    }
    .subtitle { margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--muted); }
    .updated {
      display: inline-flex;
      margin-top: 22px;
      padding: 7px 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: .85rem;
    }
    .notice {
      margin: 30px 0 36px;
      padding: 18px 20px;
      border: 1px solid #dce5ff;
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
    }
    .notice strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    h2 {
      margin: 36px 0 10px;
      font-size: 1.22rem;
      line-height: 1.35;
      letter-spacing: -.015em;
    }
    p { margin: 10px 0; }
    ul { margin: 10px 0 14px; padding-left: 1.35rem; }
    li { margin: 6px 0; }
    a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
    .contact {
      margin-top: 14px;
      padding: 18px 20px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: #fbfcfe;
    }
    .footer {
      margin-top: 30px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: .88rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      main { width: min(calc(100% - 20px), var(--max)); margin: 20px auto; }
      .document { border-radius: 14px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="topbar" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <main>
    <article class="document">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">PerianDevelopment</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">For <strong>Bouncy Cars</strong>, the mobile game published by PerianDevelopment.</p>
        <span class="updated">Last updated: 25 November 2026</span>
      </header>

      <aside class="notice">
        <strong>At a glance</strong>
        The game does not include separate third-party analytics, attribution, or tracking services operated by the developer. It does use Google Mobile Ads to show advertisements. That advertising SDK processes certain device and usage information as described below.
      </aside>

      <section>
        <h2>1. Who operates the game?</h2>
        <p><strong>Bouncy Cars</strong> is published by <strong>PerianDevelopment</strong> ("we", "us", or "our"). This Privacy Policy explains how information may be processed when you play the game on an Android device.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Information processed by the game and its advertising provider</h2>
        <p>We do not add separate third-party analytics, advertising-attribution, or tracking SDKs to the game. The game does, however, integrate the <strong>Google Mobile Ads SDK</strong> to display ads, including interstitial advertisements and optional rewarded video advertisements.</p>
        <p>Google's Mobile Ads SDK may automatically collect and share the following categories of information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>IP address:</strong> may be used to estimate the device's general location.</li>
          <li><strong>App and ad interactions:</strong> interactions such as app launches, taps, and video views.</li>
          <li><strong>Diagnostics and performance information:</strong> information about app or SDK performance, such as app launch time, hang rate, and energy usage.</li>
          <li><strong>Device and account identifiers:</strong> Android advertising ID, App Set ID and, where applicable, other identifiers associated with accounts signed in on the device.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Google describes these data practices as supporting advertising, analytics, and fraud prevention. The precise processing can depend on the SDK version, features used, device settings, and the privacy choices available in your region. Google states that data collected by the Google Mobile Ads Unity Plugin is encrypted in transit using TLS.</p>
        <p>For Google's current technical disclosure, see <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/unity/privacy/play-data-disclosure" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Mobile Ads Unity Plugin — Google Play data disclosure</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Why this information is processed</h2>
        <p>The Google Mobile Ads SDK processes information to request and deliver advertisements, measure ad and app interactions, help prevent invalid activity and advertising fraud, and support the operation and performance of its advertising services. Depending on applicable law, your consent choices, and available settings, ads may be personalized or non-personalized.</p>
        <p>We do not use a separate analytics service to build our own player profiles or track players across apps or websites.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Consent and advertising choices</h2>
        <p>Where required, we use Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) to present privacy and consent choices before requesting ads. The choices presented may depend on your location and applicable requirements. You can make or update choices through the consent options made available in the game.</p>
        <p>Android also provides settings for resetting or deleting the advertising ID and managing ad privacy. The availability and names of these settings can vary by Android version and device. You can learn more in <a href="https://support.google.com/android/answer/13314321" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's information about advertising privacy on Android</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Who receives the information?</h2>
        <p>Information processed by the Google Mobile Ads SDK is transmitted to Google and may be shared by Google with service providers or advertising partners as needed to provide, measure, protect, and improve advertising services, subject to the applicable settings, consent choices, and Google's terms and policies.</p>
        <p>Google's privacy information is available at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Data retention and security</h2>
        <p>We do not operate a separate advertising or analytics database containing the SDK data described in this policy. Google determines how long information processed through its advertising services is retained, in accordance with its policies and applicable legal requirements.</p>
        <p>Google states that information collected by the Google Mobile Ads Unity Plugin is encrypted in transit using Transport Layer Security (TLS). No method of electronic transmission or storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Children's privacy and intended audience</h2>
        <p>The game is intended for a general audience and is not specifically designed for or directed to children. We do not knowingly use the game to collect personal information directly from children. Advertising settings and SDK configurations must be kept appropriate for the game's declared target audience and the requirements of applicable laws and app-store policies.</p>
        <p>If the intended audience or the game's advertising configuration changes, this policy may be updated to reflect those changes.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Your privacy rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information, or to object to or restrict certain processing. To contact us about the game or this policy, use the email address below.</p>
        <p>Some information is processed by Google through its advertising services. Requests relating to information Google processes may also need to be made directly to Google through its <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/data-and-privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy and account controls</a>.</p>
        <p>If you are in the European Economic Area, you may also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy if the game, its advertising configuration, applicable requirements, or the services it uses change. The latest version will be published at the same address, with the updated date shown at the top of the page.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>For privacy-related questions or requests, contact:</p>
        <div class="contact">
          <strong>PerianDevelopment</strong><br>
          Email: <a href="mailto:periandevelopment+privacy@gmail.com">periandevelopment+privacy@gmail.com</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer class="footer">
        This policy describes the game's intended configuration as currently understood. The publisher is responsible for ensuring that the final app, SDK versions, consent setup, and Google Play Data safety declarations match the actual release build.
      </footer>
    </article>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
